text:
Maria Chen: Quick accessibility pass on Metrics dashboard — ran a keyboard + NVDA sweep and found a few regressions. Posting notes so we can triage.

Ashok Patel: thanks for doing this! can you list the top blockers?

Maria Chen: main things: 1) live updates to the small sparkline chart are being read repeatedly by NVDA (very noisy). 2) the orange/teal line colors on the compact charts fail contrast at small weights. 3) keyboard trap in the 'Add filter' modal when the typeahead dropdown opens (focus doesn't return to close button). 4) the long table of runs lacks a table summary/aria-describedby. 5) several icon-only buttons don't have aria-labels.

Devon S.: for the chart updates — are we using aria-live on the chart container? if it's set to assertive that could explain the repeated announcements.

Maria Chen: yep, current snippet in components/Chart.tsx sets `aria-live="assertive"` on the svg wrapper. NVDA announces every websocket tick. suggestion: change to polite + debounce updates, and only announce summary lines (e.g., "Metrics updated: 3 series changed").

Eva Li: Agree. small code suggestion:

```
// in Chart.tsx
const [announceQueue, setAnnounceQueue] = useState([]);
useEffect(() => {
  const debounced = debounce(() => {
    const summary = summarizeUpdates(announceQueue);
    setLiveMessage(summary);
    setAnnounceQueue([]);
  }, 800);
  debounced();
  return () => debounced.cancel();
}, [announceQueue]);

// render
<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{liveMessage}</div>
```

Ashok Patel: +1 to polite + debounce. Also set aria-hidden on chart elements that aren’t relevant to the screen reader (e.g., decorative gradients).

Maria Chen: contrast — the orange is `#ff8a3d` and the teal is `#1fb6b3`. on the 56px-wide mini chart they drop under 3:1 against the white bg. WCAG AA needs 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text but these lines are thin and semantic. can we pick stronger values or add an outline?

Devon S.: I ran the numbers quickly: `#ff8a3d` vs `#ffffff` ≈ 2.9:1, `#1fb6b3` vs `#ffffff` ≈ 3.1:1. propose `#ff5a00` (≈4.8:1) and `#0f9c8a` (≈5.1:1). will push a visual test in storybook.

Eva Li: for thin lines we should add a subtle 1px darker stroke for focus / emphasis states. also ensure focus-visible on the legend items (keyboard nav).

Maria Chen: keyboard trap: when you open Add filter (Cmd+K -> 'Add filter'), the typeahead dropdown moves focus into the list that is rendered in a portal — closing via Esc works but focus doesn't return to the modal close button. steps to repro included.

Devon S.: sounds like focus restoration isn't bound to modal lifecycle. if the typeahead portal mounts, it should register a focusable sentinel and on close restore to the element that opened it. I'll add a fix.

Ashok Patel: also check tab order when dropdown visible — tab should move into the list, shift+tab back to the trigger; nothing should trap keyboard.

Maria Chen: table of runs — NVDA reads column headers but there's no table summary. suggestion: add `aria-describedby` pointing to a visually-hidden summary element that says "Table lists recent model runs; columns: id, status, tokens, latency".

Eva Li: agree. For icon-only action buttons in each row (view, retry) add `aria-label="View run details"` etc. some are only title attribute right now.

Ashok Patel: quick priority: 1) chart live region change (polite + debounce + limit announcements) 2) keyboard trap fix in typeahead portal 3) color swap for contrast 4) aria-labels + table summary 5) storybook cases + NVDA smoke test.

Maria Chen: timeline: can we get hotfixes for 1 and 2 this sprint? both are causing bad UX in the wild. @Devon can you own 2? @Ashok can you do 1 and 3? I'll handle 4 and 5 and write the smoke test steps.

Devon S.: taking 2 — will add sentinel + focus restoration PR. ETA: tomorrow morning.

Ashok Patel: taking 1 + 3. will send a small PR with color tokens and change to aria-live/perf debouncing. aiming for EOD.

Maria Chen: thanks. I'll add the NVDA test steps in the ticket and attach a short recording. :thumbsup:

a11y-bot: automated check — new contrast tokens `#ff5a00` and `#0f9c8a` pass WCAG AA for normal text against #ffffff.

Eva Li: tiny copy nit — the toolbar "Collapse" button should be "Collapse panel" for clearer speech output. small change but helps SR users.

Maria Chen: good catch, adding to list.

Ashok Patel: will include that label change in the PR.

Maria Chen: ok closing loop — will file a single consolidated ticket with the above list and link PRs. thanks everyone!
